+# Source-only reconstruction and receipt notes
+
+## Exact base and package boundary
+
+Apply the accompanying source-only patch to A-Life commit
+`32e109372be39a19cabf7d9fc7cbcd9ca7c91c19` (tree prefix `b8089fc1`). The Rust
+source is byte-for-byte identical to the tested candidate at commit
+`66e733f349230a63ad91a2f87072b4405eaa99b3`. The follow-up changes only the prose
+and adds this note. The delivered patch header identifies the final cleaned
+commit and exact base.
+
+The patch includes seven Rust source/test files:
+
+- `crates/alife_training/examples/support/grounded_care_reference_v1.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_host_envelope.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_host_fixture.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_host_food_tests.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_host_loop.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_host_tests.rs`
+- `crates/alife_training/src/cpu/grouped_source_diagnosis.rs`
+
+It also includes this note, `README.md` and `RESULTS.md` from the same experiment
+directory. It excludes JSON summaries, raw diagnostics, compressed captures,
+logs, checksum manifests, generated executables and private checkpoints. The
+diagnostic tests are source code; they do not contain an imported creature life
+or learned checkpoint. This is an incremental patch, not a standalone project
+or a copy of the full evidence archive. Historical artifact references in the
+prose are intentionally not bundled.
+
+## Reconstruction
+
+1. Create a clean checkout or worktree at the exact base commit above.
+2. Run `git apply --check /path/to/m2-care-reference-source-only.patch`.
+3. Apply it with `git apply /path/to/m2-care-reference-source-only.patch`.
+4. Read the repository's applicable `AGENTS.md` files before further work.
+5. Use `grouped_host_fixture::build_matched_reference(SEED, true)` to construct
+   the fresh candidate. The ordinary `build(SEED, true)` retains the baseline.
+
+The declared fixture seed is `0x0347_5250_484F_5354`. This is the existing
+GRPHOST unit fixture, not an actual-study seed. Source construction is
+deterministic; its target asset digest, phenotype and genotype hash are in
+`RESULTS.md`. No checkpoint is needed to reconstruct the fresh authored source.
+
+The earlier verification commands and results are documented in `RESULTS.md`.
+This packaging follow-up ran no native build, test, world fixture or new life.
+A recipient who chooses to reproduce tests should use the established
+single-job offline environment with incremental compilation disabled, dev/test
+debug level 0, no optimization override and 1 test thread. The focused test
+filter is `grouped_taste_reference_`. Such reproduction is separate work, not a
+claim that this source-only package includes new measurements.
+
+## Readable compact-summary labels
+
+The original machine-readable summary files are immutable historical artifacts.
+Their keys and labels have not been rewritten. Read them as follows:
+
+- `old1` / `new1`: baseline / candidate at source iteration 1.
+- `old48` / `new48`: baseline / candidate at source iteration 48.
+- `new_min`: the candidate's minimum over the 48 source iterations.
+- Three-value contrast arrays: Ingest, summed Avoid, then Contact contrast.
+- `synthetic_hunger_0`: synthetic encoded hunger 0, with receptors held fixed.
+- `synthetic_hunger_0.35`: synthetic encoded hunger 0.35.
+- `synthetic_hunger_0.9`: synthetic encoded hunger 0.9.
+- `synthetic_fear_*` and `synthetic_pain_*`: the analogous fixed-receptor fear
+  and pain controls. These are not interventions on a living body's physiology.
+- `source_s_ingest_by_decision`: pure source S for Ingest at each actual decision.
+- `aggregate_s_i_m_c_ingest_by_decision`: combined S + I + M + C, not pure S.
+- `identity_and_work`: source-binding checks and derived charged-work counters,
+  not measured CPU instructions or elapsed cost.
+
+## Address-label errata
+
+The initial six-row candidate receipt in `REFERENCE_PROBE_V1.json.gz` has
+incorrect logical labels at `candidate_metadata.source_revision.edits[*].address`.
+The same initial labels occur in the local uncompressed copy and the original
+probe output from which it was extracted. The six affected packed rows are
+7670, 7840, 7850, 10485, 10489 and 10493. Their physical route/source/target
+triples and weight values were correct throughout. The error came from
+indexing a logical-address-sorted map by packed row.
+
+Those six labels were corrected by looking up `packed_index`. Correct labels
+appear in `REFERENCE_FINAL.json.gz` under
+`records.TASTE_REFERENCE_PROBE.candidate_metadata.source_revision.edits`, and in
+`REFERENCE_FINAL_SUMMARY.json` under `candidate_identity.source_revision.edits`.
+The six source weights, source identity and measured behavior did not change.
+
+A separate inherited erratum remains in recipe reader metadata:
+`reader_rows[*].address` and `reader_rows[*].grounded_address` use the same
+incorrect indexed lookup. This metadata is embedded in `SOURCE_DIAG.json.gz`,
+`REFERENCE_PROBE_V1.json.gz` and the full candidate metadata in
+`REFERENCE_FINAL.json.gz`. Those reader labels were deliberately not rewritten;
+their historical recipe hashes are preserved. Do not use them as authoritative
+logical addresses. Resolve the saved packed indices through the phenotype's
+persistent address map instead. This erratum concerns labels, not the selected
+reader rows or their coefficients.
+
+## Historical checksum preservation
+
+All original JSON files, compressed captures, logs and historical receipts
+remain byte-for-byte unchanged from commit
+`66e733f349230a63ad91a2f87072b4405eaa99b3`. The original `SHA256SUMS` is also
+unchanged. Its README and RESULTS hashes identify the original prose at that
+commit, so they intentionally do not describe the later cleaned wording.
+All other entries still verify. The source-only patch omits that historical
+manifest rather than presenting it as a checksum of the cleaned package.
